{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Data Flow Diagram, Facts and Its History"}, {"type": "position", "content": 1}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 3}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when you talk about flow diagrams."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe common activities at work by using short sentences in familiar spoken and written situations. Interpret the requirements report to determine the technological needs in managing information, based on rules and protocols established by the company."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Participates in simple conversations or simulated situations about the communicative topics for this level through the appropriate use of simple pronunciation aspects, and grammar and vocabulary structures."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Recognizes simple ideas on requirement reports, tools for Object Oriented Programming, and other basic programming tools."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n3le03ob01re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Read about DFD."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write down on you notebook its origin, definition, and some important facts about it. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Draw an example of a DFD in ADSI."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Present your work to your classmates and check pronunciation with your instructor. "}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I talk about different facts related to data flow diagrams"}, {"type": "text", "content": "I give information related the history of data flow diagrams."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I explain the importance of flow diagrams."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "flow "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a continuous movement of something "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Besides, it shows the interaction between elements, so that, if we develop a flow diagram, we structure and order this complex system. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le03ob01aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "develop"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to grow or improve"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I think we developed an analysis of the information system  5 years ago. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le03ob01aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "input "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the data that enters a computer or a machine for a process "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: If we develop a data flow diagram, we know what kind of information is input to and output from the system. ."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le03ob01aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "output "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the result of a process"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: If we develop a data flow diagram, we know what information belongs to the input and what to the output in the system."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le03ob01aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "timing "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the control of the speed in a process or event"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: However, if you want information about the timing of the process or the sequence, the DFD doesn't show these elements."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le03ob01aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "store "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to collect or copy information to keep it "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: This is important because it also shows the data stored and provides a visualization of data processing. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le03ob01aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Zero Conditional In Affirmative And Negative"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the zero conditional to talk about real situations and facts. You can use the zero conditional in both negative and affirmative statements. </br> </br> You use the next structure to explain two situations that complement each other and that are always real. <br/><br/>  Structure: <span class=\"strong\"> If + Present Simple, Present Simple </span><br/><br/>  For example: <br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\"> If we <span class=\"strong\"> want </span> to represent processes in an efficient way, we <span class=\"strong\"> use </span> the data flow diagrams. </span> <br/><br/>  The first part explains a <span class=\"strong\"> condition </span> and the second one explains the <span class=\"strong\"> result </span>, consequence or direct relation to the first condition. Both parts need to be in present simple and they are always about true situations that are obvious or general. <br/><br/>  One or both of the parts of the sentence can be a negative statement. Remember to use the auxiliary verbs when necessary. <br/><br/>  Structure: <span class=\"strong\"> If + Present Simple (negative), + Present Simple (negative).</span><br/><br/>   For example: <br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\"> If you don't use </span> a graphical representation of how the data flows, <span class=\"strong\"> you don't get </span> a general sketch of the system. </span><br/><br/>  Notice that the clauses are separated by a comma; when the sentence starts with the phrase expressing the consequence, do not use the comma to separate them. Look at the example: <br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\"> You get </span> a general sketch of the system <span class=\"strong\"> if you use </span> a graphical representation of how the data flows.</span> <br/><br/>   You can also replace <span class=\"strong\"> If </span> by <span class=\"strong\"> when </span> without changing the meaning of the sentence."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If we develop a data flow diagram, we know what kind of information is input to and output from the system. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "If you want information about the timing of the process or the sequence, the DFD doesn't show these elements. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "If we develop a flow diagram, we can structure and order this complex system. "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Addie Model"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use an Addie model to create an effective training and performance of a process."}, {"type": "text", "content": "In an ADDIE framework, you can find 5 phases of a generic process. Instructional designers and training developers use this model to have a guideline for effective performance. The objective is to have a constant revision or feedback of the specific process.  The ADDIE model is dynamic and interactive. Let's take a look at the description of its phases. <br/><br/>  <li> <span class=\"strong\"> Analysis:</span> In this phase, the designer identifies the objectives and possible problems. Also, he needs to analyze the environment, the advantages, and disadvantages.</li>  <li> <span class=\"strong\"> Design: </span> The instructional designer plans strategies to fulfill the objectives.  This phase needs to be specific and systematic, this means it has to be organized and logical.</li>  <li> <span class=\"strong\"> Development:</span> It is the moment to create and develop the designs. The developers can include more elements according to the analysis and design. Also, they can revise and give feedback to the process. </li>   <li> <span class=\"strong\"> Implementation: </span> In this phase, the designers apply the procedures and elements developed. At the same time, they test and analyze its application.  </li>   <li> <span class=\"strong\"> Evaluation: </span> The evaluation of the process is the most important element. Remember you can find this phase in the others; it can be formative and summative.</li>"}, {"type": "image", "content": "enpe8n3le03ob01img01.jpg"}], "type": "learning_points"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about different facts related to data flow diagrams."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can give information related to the history of data flow diagrams."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can explain the importance of flow diagrams."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "How can you show or represent a process easily? Give some examples."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Where can you find flow diagrams? "}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "The Importance of Flow Diagrams in Data Processing"}], "id": 0, "img_pat