: ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment."}], "type": "post_instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Listening"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Reading"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Writing"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Speaking"}], "type": "learning_skills"}], "id": 11}], "stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "id": 0, "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe8n3le03ob01re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "enpe8n3le03ob01re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<span class=\"strong\"> Technician:</span> I just completed a full analysis of the information system that the company had 2 years ago. So, last month I found serious problems with some processes in the company. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\"> Operator:</span> What do you mean? <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\"> Technician:</span> First, the company has a lot of information for each process. It is necessary to organize the data. If we want to represent processes in an efficient way, we need to use data flow diagrams. I think we developed one 5 years ago."}, {"time": "29000", "image": "enpe8n3le03ob01re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\"> Operator:</span> Sorry, I don't know what that is. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\"> Technician:</span> A data flow diagram, or DFD, is a graphic representation of the flow of data, with the support of an information system. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\"> Operator:</span> Ok, that is something new. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\"> Technician:</span> It is not! Four decades ago, Larry Constantine proposed the concept of DFD. For its development, he took the Data Flow Graph model of computation. In the year 1970, Data Flow Diagrams became a systematic and popular way to see how a project evolves step by step. A few years later, people used the model to present data flow in computers. That was a very important fact for software development."}, {"time": "74000", "image": "enpe8n3le03ob01re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\"> Operator:</span> I see. So, do you think we need to design a new DFD? <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\"> Technician:</span> That seems to be the solution. If we develop a data flow diagram, we know what kind of information is input to and output from the system. This is important because it also shows the stored data and provides a visualization of data processing. However, if you want information about the timing of the process or the sequence, the DFD doesn't show these elements. But, we can use an ADDIE model. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\"> Operator:</span> This seems to be useful for organizing information. Besides, it shows the interaction between elements, so that if we develop a flow diagram, we can structure and order this complex system."}], "coverimg": "enpe8n3le03ob01re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "title": ""}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}], "type": "lab_options"}], "type": "scholar"}]}